 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Most bikes have a frame size chart in their warranty manual, or you can measure yourself and compare to standards on a seat tube measurement. You should feel a gentle bend in your knees when pedaling, not straight out. If you' too short or too tall, it'll affect that. Say you too short for the right size bike, a shorter reach crank set is much simpler than switching to shorter frame. Then a shorter crank might make it feel right. Then a longer frame might be worth trying. Some people don't, especially if they stand bit. It depends how high you like to sit.",
